- Disable normalization for project name (#4148)
- Find shortest matches for schemanames

### Perf:
- Cache sorted table results
- Predefine regexes for sort/filter
- Model class support - Proxies are about 1/4th the speed of native property access in Chrome, and 1/100th in Firefox/Safari.

### Cleanup:
- emphasizeBody is never used
- Consistent @ import instead of ~

# Model class support:
- Class file model support
- Rename models
- Convert some models
- Separate Norman and Steve base classes
- Switch json-path libraries for SSR

Models can now be defined as an ES6 class in `models/[type].class.js` instead of a sack of things on a Proxy object.

```javascript
import SteveModel from '@/plugins/steve/steve-class';         // Most models should extend this for Steve APIs (/v1)
// import NormanModel from '@/plugins/steve/norman-class';    // Or this for Norman APIs (/v3)
// import { Resource } from '@/plugins/steve/resource-class'; // This is the base class that both extend

export default class Widget extends SteveModel {
  get someValue() {
    // computed property
    return 42;
  }

  someMethod() {
    // instance method
    doStuff();
  }
}
```

- If present, the new .class file takes precendence over old proxy implementation.
- If there is no `models/` file present at all, the appropriate one (Steve or Norman) is guessed (Proxies are not used).
- Classes work like normal to add more behavior, you can extend, call super, etc.
- To convert the old implementation you mostly change `property() { ... }` -> `get property() { ... }` and `method() { return () => { ... } }` to `method() { ... }`.  And trailing commas aren't allowed between class members.j
- The base `Resource` should not have any fields defined that conflict with any key ever returned by the APIs (e.g. name, description, state, etc used to be a problem).  Additional stuff may need to be moved out of here to handle additional projects.
- The `SteveModel` and `NormanModel` know how to handle those keys separately now, so the computed name/description/etc is only in the Steve implementation.  Shenanigans like rewriting these to `_name` back and forth are gone.
- Only some of the common high-volume models have been converted, and the generic usages.  The rest should be moved over and then support for the old stuff dropped to get rid of some overhead.
- Much of resource-instance is mostly duplicated into resource-class.  If you change one you probably need a corresponding change in the other until Proxies are dropped.

**Notice**: This PR tweaks the structure of how hooks are created and updates some of the event names. Please update your custom hooks if you were relying on any.

---

New syntax for hook registration:

```js
export default ({ filter, action, init, schedule }) => {
  filter('items.create', () => {
    console.log('Creating Item!');
  });

  action('items.create', () => {
    console.log('Item created!');
  });

  init('app.before', () => {
    console.log('Hello there!');
  });

  schedule('*/5 * * * * *', () => {
    console.log('Surprise!');
  });
};
```

Thanks to @smilledge who came up with the initial idea [here](https://github.com/directus/directus/discussions/7744#discussioncomment-1288090) and [here](https://github.com/directus/directus/discussions/7843).

**Please describe the changes this PR makes and why it should be merged:**
This PR fixes the following:
- Problem with global slash commands greying out when they should not be.
- Problem in the `GCommandLoader` resulting in a error (`error.response.status`).

This PR adds the following features:
- `loadFromCache` option in the `GCommandsClient#commands`, this feature disables/enables loading from cache.

```js
// This will load from cache
new GCommandsClient({
    ...options
    commands: {
        loadFromCache: true, // loadFromCache is set to true by default
    }
});

// This will not load from cache
new GCommandsClient({
    ...options
    commands: {
        loadFromCache: false,
    }
});
```

